 "notes": [
  [
   "Power: the switch common is the 3.3 V rail (XIAO 3V3 pin and the LEDs). Position 1 = badge 3.3 V feeds the rail. Position 2 (OFF) and position 3 (USB / BAT) leave the badge disconnected.",
   [
    38.1,
    96.52
   ]
  ],
  [
   "On USB or a LiPo the XIAO powers the rail itself. In OFF the switch ties D1 to the rail so the firmware can blank the LEDs and sleep (the module itself has no off switch).",
   [
    38.1,
    100.33
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Do not plug in USB with the switch on SAO while on a badge: two 3.3 V regulators would share one rail.",
   [
    38.1,
    104.14
   ]
  ],
  [
   "J2 is a LiPo connector wired to the XIAO's battery pads (two pad positions under the module: C3/S3 and C6). The XIAO charges the cell from USB-C. No coin cell on this board.",
   [
    38.1,
    107.95
   ]
  ],
  [
   "D1..D5 = SK6805 side-firing RGB, chained D1 (pink ghost, right) to D5 (Pac-Man, left). One 100 nF per gap. R2, R3: 330 ohm on the SAO GPIO pins per docs/standard.md.",
   [
    38.1,
    111.76
   ]
  ],
  [
   "Mode button = the XIAO's own BOOT button (no extra part).",
   [
    38.1,
    115.57
   ]
  ]
 ]
}